with soma frictional games is leaving  behind the world of amnesia and  venturing into a new setting and new  thematic territory this horror sci fi  game delves into fuse of consciousness  and instead of assaulting you with a  barrage of jump-scares soma goes for a  slow build up trying to get inside your  head you play as Simon a man who has  found himself in an abandoned science  facility Thomas grip of frictional games  says that the environments should be a  narrative playground filled with clues  that help you better understand the  game's world and piece together the  story of what's happened in these places  I love environmental storytelling so  when I played a section of the game  recently I wanted to examine every sign  and every schematic but the game is also  designed to pull in players who don't  want to investigate every little detail  players who prefer to just charge  through the game without reading  anything should still get the main gist  of the story that story remains shrouded  in mystery but a few details emerge from  my time with the game something strange  has happened with the robots in the  science facility I explored somehow it  seemed that the consciousnesses of  humans were becoming imprisoned in the  metal bodies of automatons and although  I initially thought the game might be  set in space or on a distant alien world  it actually takes place below the  surface of one of Earth's own oceans it  was as I made my way across the ocean  floor that soma started to scare me  there were noises that sounded like  distant screams and I wasn't sure if my  imagination was making more of the  muffled ocean sounds than was actually  there later making my way through the  flooded wreckage of the lambda station I  encountered the qianxi a mysterious  ghostly threat who you must hide or run  from the section of soma that I played  really was a slow build letting the  atmosphere and the sounds create a sense  of psychological fear rather than  relying on gore or jump scares I admit  I'm scared to return to somas unsettling  world but I also looked forward to  spending more time in its environments  looking at all the little details that  would help me piece together its  narrative soma is aiming for a release  on PC and ps4 in early 2015
 

